#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Self-validating Simplified->Traditional map (cycle 1180 codification).

Replaces the hand-built differing-pairs PAIRS tables that collapsed to ZERO
entries through Python implicit adjacent-string concatenation, so the simplified
scan iterated an empty table and reported CLEAN for three consecutive cycles
(1177/1178/1179) while 87 records leaked Simplified script onto the page.

Why the dict form cannot collapse:
  * Python does NOT implicitly concatenate strings across parenthesised dict
    entries -- each "s": "T" pair is a separate literal with an explicit key.
  * The differing-pairs invariant (s != T) is asserted for EVERY entry, so a
    Traditional-legal char that self-maps (e.g. 台) cannot enter the table.
  * Import-time assertions mean a broken table fails LOUDLY instead of
    reporting a false clean.

Usage:
    from s2t_map import DIFF
    hits = [c for c in text if c in DIFF]
"""

